            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0604" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760F.62/805: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-14T16:00:00-03:00">September 14, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 14—2:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>213. President Vargas, who is much concerned of course over the recent trend of
                    events in Europe, asks me if I can ascertain as soon as <pb facs="0605" n="597"
                        xml:id="pg597"/> possible very confidentially from you anything of the
                    Department’s opinion and attitude in the face of the present situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
